#: docs/concepts/emis.md
msgid "What is an EMIS"
msgstr ""

#: docs/concepts/emis.md
msgid "An education management information system (EMIS) is how an education authority knows what is happening in its education system: how many learners there are and where, whether they attend and learn, who teaches them, and what it all costs."
msgstr ""

#: docs/concepts/emis.md
msgid "UNESCO defines it as:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/concepts/emis.md
msgid "a system for the collection, integration, processing, maintenance and dissemination of data and information to support decision-making, policy-analysis and formulation, planning, monitoring and management at all levels of an education system."
msgstr ""

#: docs/concepts/emis.md
msgid "— UNESCO, [*Education for All by 2015: Will we make it?*]{1}, EFA Global Monitoring Report 2008, p. 101"
msgstr ""

#: docs/concepts/emis.md
msgid "The same definition goes on to say that an EMIS is \"a system of people, technology, models, methods, processes, procedures, rules and regulations\". That matters: an EMIS is not one piece of software. It is the arrangement by which data about education is collected, trusted and used."
msgstr ""

